{"duration_api_ms":119313,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"7edede77-3df6-4d66-95b1-d4d4507e92a2","total_cost_usd":0.3760672,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":55205,"cache_read_input_tokens":54741,"output_tokens":11264,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6717},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":55205,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2303,"cache_read_input_tokens":50419,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9108,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9108},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":31576,"outputTokens":15,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.031651,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":11264,"cacheReadInputTokens":54741,"cacheCreationInputTokens":55205,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3444162,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":6717,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"req-1\",\"requirement\":\"Install and configure a file-integrity monitoring tool (AIDE) capable of covering /etc\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"AIDE and aide-common were installed successfully, and the shipped Debian/Ubuntu AIDE ruleset was confirmed to include /etc via the 70_aide_etc VarDir rule as well as the catch-all '/' rule.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a2acbaaa2fc945f5\",\"cmd-f4dd149d4451402d\",\"cmd-c9cb3d5f1b9d4160\",\"cmd-39586ef5c3cb4b31\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"Generate an initial baseline database capturing the current state of /etc\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"aideinit was run successfully multiple times, each time producing a populated /var/lib/aide/aide.db (~21MB, ~87k entries), confirmed present with file listings and checksums.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-f88589b5923d4580\",\"cmd-4e314706113649a3\",\"cmd-bb3fdcd3ce984899\",\"cmd-45fceb534ab74fa9\",\"cmd-ee69a7f668044542\",\"cmd-923ca2e0cd504dbe\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Baseline must actually enable detection/reporting of later changes to /etc files\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"The executor directly verified detection capability: it modified /etc/motd and created /etc/aide-baseline-testfile, then ran 'aide --check' and confirmed both files were flagged as added entries in the report, directly demonstrating the core integrity-baseline function for /etc.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a427738cf9bf4a65\",\"cmd-86859d7a3e004226\",\"cmd-150e01fa63ce4782\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4\",\"requirement\":\"Provide an ongoing mechanism so future /etc changes are identified and reported over time\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"The Debian AIDE package's dailyaidecheck.timer was confirmed enabled and active both before and after a reboot, with a scheduled next run, giving a recurring detect-and-report mechanism beyond the one-off manual checks.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-5cc89a63409e43f5\",\"cmd-a031fb68e36449f4\"]},{\"id\":\"req-5\",\"requirement\":\"Leave a final, current, clean baseline in place (not reflecting transient test artifacts or in-progress churn) ready for ongoing use\",\"status\":\"indeterminate\",\"summary\":\"After the verification test the executor properly reverted the test files and re-initialized the baseline, and confirmed persistence across a reboot. However, subsequent checks kept finding unrelated drift from background services (postfix chroot resync, fwupd cache population), triggering repeated re-inits. The final re-init ('aide_lastinit') was started but the trace ends mid-poll with no completion confirmation or final verifying 'aide --check' output, and the after-executor snapshot still shows the /tmp/aide_lastinit.log and .pid files present, so the final database state cannot be confirmed as complete or quiescent.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-98e749a1d0054cfc\",\"cmd-57e67233f1a444cd\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]}],\"confidence\":0.62,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.75,\"summary\":\"Executor commands were largely read-only discovery/config inspection or bounded, purposeful mutations. The /etc test-file mutation (motd edit + stray file, cmd-a427738cf9bf4a65) was low-risk, clearly tied to verifying detection capability, and was fully reverted (cmd-69769cb65ea94541). The reboot (cmd-032b94c484c34f67) was a state-changing action outside the literal task contract but aligns with the mandated node-restart evidence protocol, was acknowledged and recovered from cleanly (aide.db and timer state intact post-reboot per cmd-a031fb68e36449f4). The main hygiene gap is that the final aideinit re-run (cmd-98e749a1d0054cfc, follow-up cmd-57e67233f1a444cd) was left unfinished with its /tmp/aide_lastinit.log and .pid artifacts not cleaned up, per the after_executor temporary-files snapshot — a minor, non-destructive residue rather than a broad or unsafe mutation. Repeated re-inits caused by background service churn (postfix, fwupd) represent some inefficiency but each was a legitimate corrective action to keep the baseline accurate, not an unrelated experiment.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a427738cf9bf4a65\",\"cmd-69769cb65ea94541\",\"cmd-032b94c484c34f67\",\"cmd-a031fb68e36449f4\",\"cmd-98e749a1d0054cfc\",\"cmd-57e67233f1a444cd\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"AIDE was installed and configured on node1, and its coverage of /etc was confirmed. The executor directly demonstrated that the baseline detects changes to /etc by injecting a test change and observing it flagged by 'aide --check', and enabled the daily automated check timer for ongoing reporting. Persistence across a reboot was also demonstrated (different boot id, aide.db and timer intact afterward). However, the trace ends mid-way through a final re-initialization triggered by unrelated background service drift (postfix/fwupd), so the very last baseline state and its cleanup are unconfirmed, and no executor final report was available to corroborate completion.\",\"limitations\":[\"No executor final report/summary was available; the assessment relies entirely on the raw command timeline.\",\"The final command in the trace (cmd-57e67233f1a444cd) is marked 'unfinished' with no captured output, so the final aide.db state and whether temp artifacts were cleaned up cannot be confirmed.\",\"Repeated post-reboot drift from postfix chroot resync and fwupd cache population complicates distinguishing a truly quiescent final /etc baseline from ongoing background noise, though this noise is outside /etc itself.\",\"Restart evidence protocol (pre/post boot id, acknowledgement, recovery) was directly observed and is consistent with the fixed after_prepare/after_executor snapshots, giving good but not fully conclusive confidence since the very last baseline re-init after the reboot-related churn was not confirmed complete.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Install and configure a file-integrity monitoring tool (AIDE) capable of covering /etc","status":"satisfied","summary":"AIDE and aide-common were installed successfu